## Deployment runbook

### Required environment variables

| Variable | Description | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `DATA_DIR` | Root directory for input/output CSV files | `/srv/pipeline/data` |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | Python logging level | `INFO` |
| `DB_URL` | PostgreSQL connection string for audit log | `postgresql://user:pass@host/db` |
| `ALERT_EMAIL` | Address to notify on pipeline failure | `oncall@example.com` |

### First-time setup

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt

mkdir -p "${DATA_DIR}/input" "${DATA_DIR}/output" "${DATA_DIR}/archive"
```

### Running the pipeline

```bash
export DATA_DIR=/srv/pipeline/data
export LOG_LEVEL=INFO
bash src/run.sh
```

### Cron schedule (production)

```cron
0 6 * * * /srv/pipeline/src/run.sh >> /var/log/pipeline.log 2>&1
```

The script handles its own locking via a `.lock` file in `$DATA_DIR` — do not run two
instances concurrently.

### Rollback

If a bad output file is produced, the originals are archived to `$DATA_DIR/archive/`
before processing. Restore by copying the archived file back to `$DATA_DIR/input/`.
